WEBVTT

NOTE The Kid Brother (1927) - Riah TV captions

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.500
[music]

00:01:54.250 --> 00:01:59.500
"'Flash,' I'm sorry I let you
persuade me to keep on with the
show."

00:02:01.750 --> 00:02:07.250
"Forget it, Mary. It wouldn't be
a show without you. Besides,
everything's going to be O.K."

00:04:29.500 --> 00:04:34.000
We'll be leaving for the meeting
directly — how about my Sunday
shirt?

00:04:39.250 --> 00:04:45.500
"If anything happens to that
shirt, young man, I'll whale the
life out of you."

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:04.500
Well, I see the town raised the
money for the dam all right.

00:08:07.000 --> 00:08:10.000
"It will be a big thing
for Hickoryville."

00:08:13.250 --> 00:08:16.000
"And a bigger thing
for you — eh, Sheriff?"

00:08:25.250 --> 00:08:33.500
"Son, how many times have I told
you we don't want any more
trouble with these Hickorys."

00:08:49.500 --> 00:08:55.000
"Where is this metropolis of
Hickoryville — and who signs the
permits for the shows there?"

00:08:57.750 --> 00:09:04.250
Sheriff Jim Hickory — but he
ain't got any use for medicine
shows — he run the last one out
of town.

00:09:54.000 --> 00:09:58.000
"You stay here, son — the town
meeting's no place for boys."

00:12:51.750 --> 00:12:52.750
"Hi, Sheriff!"

00:13:16.500 --> 00:13:22.750
"I've brought this show all the
way from New York just to play
your wonderful city."

00:13:28.000 --> 00:13:31.250
"Sheriff, I'd like you to
autograph this little permit."

00:14:18.500 --> 00:14:27.750
"I move we give Sheriff Hickory
a vote of thanks and place the
money in his keeping until it is
time to turn it over."

00:14:37.500 --> 00:14:42.500
"I appreciate your confidence,
Mr. Chairman — and I'll write
the State Treasurer tonight."

00:14:46.500 --> 00:14:50.750
"I'd rather see that much
money in a real safe place."

00:14:57.750 --> 00:15:01.250
"You're hinting that it
won't be safe with me?"

00:15:03.500 --> 00:15:08.750
"I got some money in there — and
I don't want to see it —
mislaid!"

00:16:55.500 --> 00:16:59.000
"Keep back — or someone
might get hurt."

00:17:57.250 --> 00:18:01.500
"Mr. Hickory, I — I don't
know how to thank you —"

00:18:06.000 --> 00:18:08.000
"Who told you my name?"

00:18:11.000 --> 00:18:14.250
"Everyone in this state
knows the Hickorys —"

00:18:16.250 --> 00:18:23.250
"— and I'm proud to have met the
man who made the Hickory name
famous."

00:18:33.500 --> 00:18:36.250
"You mean my father
and brothers."

00:18:41.250 --> 00:18:45.250
"You're too modest —
but I like you for it."

00:19:22.500 --> 00:19:23.500
"What's your name?"

00:19:50.000 --> 00:19:51.750
"Where do you live?"

00:19:54.750 --> 00:19:58.000
With the Medicine Show
— down by the river.

00:21:02.500 --> 00:21:07.750
"This is a great day for
Hickoryville — and we Hickorys
have something to be proud of."

00:21:13.000 --> 00:21:16.000
"Never mind the letter —
do those supper dishes."

00:23:14.500 --> 00:23:16.500
"How does that sound to you?"

00:23:38.000 --> 00:23:40.750
"Now you boys can sign it."

00:24:24.750 --> 00:24:26.500
"Goin' to the show?"

00:24:28.750 --> 00:24:32.000
"That big medicine
show in the village."

00:24:39.000 --> 00:24:42.000
"Who gave them
permission to play here?"

00:25:21.500 --> 00:25:24.000
"I thought I'd mail our letter."

00:25:29.000 --> 00:25:31.750
"Did you give them permission?"

00:25:44.750 --> 00:25:52.250
"As you seem to be taking over
the duties of sheriff — go down
and stop the show."

00:27:34.750 --> 00:27:42.811
"This medicine is not only good
for man and beast but is
recommended as a furniture
polish and for cleaning

00:27:42.821 --> 00:27:43.500
harness."

00:27:56.750 --> 00:28:02.500
"My father sent me down to stop
the show — if you don't mind."

00:28:28.500 --> 00:28:34.500
"Now, folks, on the count of
three, this trick will prove
that the little sheriff is out
of sight."

00:28:59.000 --> 00:29:03.500
"Now, folks, we will again be
entertained by our little
beauty!"

00:29:13.000 --> 00:29:16.750
"If you don't stop the show,
I'll have you arrested."

00:29:31.000 --> 00:29:32.250
"Where's your authority?"

00:30:01.750 --> 00:30:06.750
"One moment, Sheriff, I've got a
little present for you — first."

00:31:29.250 --> 00:31:34.000
"I'm giving you twenty-four
hours to get out of here!"

00:31:37.000 --> 00:31:39.000
"I'll get the key,
Mr. Hickory —"

00:31:45.000 --> 00:31:48.750
"The kid is as much
at fault as anybody."

00:31:51.750 --> 00:31:55.000
I'll attend to him
when we get home.

00:36:12.750 --> 00:36:14.750
Will these do for tonight?

00:36:50.250 --> 00:36:53.000
"Would you get me a
glass of water, please?"

00:37:11.250 --> 00:37:14.000
"Wouldn't you rather
have some hot coffee?"

00:38:44.250 --> 00:38:45.250
"It's the wind."

00:40:19.500 --> 00:40:23.250
"Me and ma have come
to take the girl home."

00:40:24.500 --> 00:40:29.250
"She can't stay here where
there's no womenfolks. It ain't
decent."

00:40:33.000 --> 00:40:35.250
"I suppose I'd better go."

00:40:48.000 --> 00:40:53.250
"Will you go with me to the
celebration for the dam
tomorrow?"

00:41:25.750 --> 00:41:30.000
"Good night, Mary — I'm
going to sleep in the barn."

00:42:06.000 --> 00:42:09.490
The money will now remain in the
Sheriff's keeping until the
celebration tomorrow,

00:42:09.500 --> 00:42:12.500
when he will turn it over to the
State officials who will be
present.

00:42:24.500 --> 00:42:26.000
"Where's that Harold?"

00:42:28.750 --> 00:42:30.500
"Sleeping in the barn."

00:42:33.000 --> 00:42:39.000
"The girl from the medicine show
came home with him. She's asleep
in the parlor."

00:43:43.250 --> 00:43:46.000
"Miss — I'm going to
fetch you some breakfast."

00:44:59.500 --> 00:45:00.750
"Everything all right, miss?"

00:45:27.000 --> 00:45:28.500
"Here's your breakfast, Miss."

00:48:00.250 --> 00:48:04.250
"Get to work — that boy Harold
does more work than both of
you."

00:49:35.000 --> 00:49:41.000
"— and if you fellows ever try
anything like that again, I
won't let you off so easy."

00:50:09.250 --> 00:50:14.000
"I'm earning my board at the
Hoopers' by helping with the
housework."

00:50:33.750 --> 00:50:35.000
"I'll get my wraps."

00:50:40.500 --> 00:50:44.750
"You go in and get her wraps — I
want to speak to her a moment."

00:51:30.500 --> 00:51:33.500
"The older he grows,
the worse he gets."

00:53:44.500 --> 00:53:47.250
"You boys better get dressed
for the celebration."

00:54:04.250 --> 00:54:07.750
"Come on, you're going with
me to the celebration."

00:54:30.250 --> 00:54:34.250
"If you don't go with me,
you won't go with anybody."

00:55:31.750 --> 00:55:34.000
"The money for the
dam has been stolen!"

00:56:03.250 --> 00:56:08.000
"All I know is — I found the
strong box open and the money
gone."

00:56:14.000 --> 00:56:20.000
"Someone broke into your house,
opened the box — and you didn't
hear nothing?"

00:56:31.000 --> 00:56:33.250
"It sounds funny to me —"

00:56:40.750 --> 00:56:43.750
"Haven't you any clue, Jim?"

00:57:04.250 --> 00:57:11.250
"I just got an idea who did this
and I'm going out and get them."

00:57:17.000 --> 00:57:24.250
"We ain't satisfied with your
goin' and I reckon you better
stay here till we are."

00:57:30.500 --> 00:57:33.250
"Then I'll deputize my sons."

00:57:40.250 --> 00:57:45.750
"Boys, it's those two fellows
with the medicine show. Bring
them back here."

00:57:55.000 --> 00:57:58.750
"Son, you might get hurt.
This is a man's job."

00:58:32.000 --> 00:58:35.250
"Harold, aren't you going
with your brothers?"

00:58:46.500 --> 00:58:54.250
"You see — my father and
brothers don't reckon much on me
— and I guess they're right."

00:58:58.500 --> 00:59:03.500
"I'm not what you think I
am. I was just pretending."

00:59:10.000 --> 00:59:14.500
"But you can be what I think
you are — without pretending."

00:59:19.250 --> 00:59:25.750
"— and no matter what anybody
else thinks, have confidence in
yourself and you can't lose."

00:59:31.500 --> 00:59:33.750
"Do you really believe in me?"

00:59:42.500 --> 00:59:47.250
"There's that girl from the
medicine show — and he's helping
her to get away."

01:00:29.750 --> 01:00:32.000
"Pop, I reckon they got away."

01:08:37.000 --> 01:08:41.000
"You keep him covered, Sheriff,
while I get the money."

01:11:11.750 --> 01:11:14.000
"Help! Help! I can't swim!"

01:14:04.250 --> 01:14:08.500
"I went clear beyond the county
line but not a trace of them."

01:14:11.750 --> 01:14:14.500
"Jim Hickory, I believe
you stole that money!"

01:17:12.500 --> 01:17:17.250
"Let's put him under arrest and
take the law in our own hands."

01:17:36.500 --> 01:17:41.500
"The leading citizen of
Hickoryville may soon find
himself at the end of his rope."

01:19:43.250 --> 01:19:45.500
"Son, you're a real Hickory!"
